    "notes": [
      "Four trades, injected one at a time so the simulator is called four times. The runner loops them and each gets its own HTML report and Excel row.",
      "All four are CNHUSD: the netting rule is configured CNH-USD, in alphabetical order, so every pair in the pack is written that way. The sheet's two USD-CNH trades are carried as CNHUSD the other way round - BNKA-HK buys 67400 CNH and pays 10000 USD, where the first two sell the same amounts - so they are the same trades, stated in the rule's order.",
      "All four run the full pipeline with no expectations declared.",
      "Amounts mirror across the two directions, 67400 CNH against 10000 USD, so the four net to zero in both currencies.",
      "partyDirection is BNKA-HK's side of CNH, so it follows the base currency buyer and seller: Sell on the first two, where BNKB-HK is the buyer, and Buy on the last two. Steps 05 / 05b then expect CNH SELL / USD BUY on Domain A for the first two and the reverse on Domain B, and steps 07 / 07b expect CNH PAYABLE / USD RECEIVABLE on Domain A for them.",
      "tradeReference, tradeReferenceSupplement and counterpartyReferenceNumber are free-text boxes, generated per run.",
      "ccpAlias, clearingBroker and counterpartyClearingBroker are blank and have no wrapper field, so they are left out of the payload.",
      "Party CCP and Cpty CCP are legal-entity reference data, not trade fields, so they are recorded here only."
    ]
